<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#hajj">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hajj</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The hajj is the pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> that every Muslim who is able is expected to make at least once in a lifetime, one of the five pillars of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Pilgrimage routes linked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a>. Pilgrimages by rulers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/askia-muhammad">Askia Muhammad</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> carried political prestige, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> lay on important pilgrim routes eastward.</p></div>
